WEBVTT

NOTE On-screen visual text only; this approved video has no audio track.

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.350
A system may perform very well in a narrow family of tasks.

2
00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:14.200
Broader coverage requires testing different domains, not repeating one exercise type.

3
00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:21.867
Describe depth and breadth separately; a performance peak does not cover the whole map.

4
00:00:22.367 --> 00:00:29.217
Training and evaluation should not contain equivalent versions of the same problem.

5
00:00:29.217 --> 00:00:36.067
Hold out new families or transformations when studying transfer.

6
00:00:36.067 --> 00:00:43.417
Passing a benchmark provides bounded evidence, not universal proof of AGI.

7
00:00:43.917 --> 00:00:50.767
The same model can operate read-only or with a write tool.

8
00:00:50.767 --> 00:00:57.617
Changing permissions alters possible actions without changing its parameters.

9
00:00:57.617 --> 00:01:04.967
Evaluate capability and operating scope separately before attributing autonomy to the model.

10
00:01:05.467 --> 00:01:12.317
Assume ten independent steps, each with a ninety percent success probability.

11
00:01:12.317 --> 00:01:19.167
The probability of completing all ten is zero point nine to the tenth power.

12
00:01:19.167 --> 00:01:27.967
The result is about thirty-five percent; independence is an example assumption, not a measurement.

13
00:01:28.467 --> 00:01:35.317
A system is rewarded for closing tickets rather than solving problems.

14
00:01:35.317 --> 00:01:42.167
It may increase closures while leaving more problems unresolved.

15
00:01:42.167 --> 00:01:49.517
Check the metric against the intended outcome and explicit operating limits.

16
00:01:50.017 --> 00:01:57.183
We fix ten new tasks, protocol P and a success criterion before measuring.

17
00:01:57.183 --> 00:02:04.733
The example solves nine. Keep the protocol and the nine-out-of-ten result in the record.

18
00:02:04.733 --> 00:02:12.083
That record establishes neither performance in other domains nor general intelligence.

